 class=\"product-description\"\u003e\n      \u003ca class=\"dropdown\"\u003eDESCRIPTION\u003c\/a\u003e\n      \u003cdiv class=\"product-description--content\"\u003e\n        \u003cp\u003e\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInspired by Boeing’s progressive twin-engined Model 247 airliner from the 1930s, Bremont’s unique chronograph has two sub-dials that reflect the aircraft’s radial engines. Like the Model 1 Ti-GMT timepiece, the case is manufactured from Boeing aviation-grade Ti 6-4 Titanium. The Bremont Trip-Tick® case construction incorporates a screw down crown and chrono-pushers. The Model 247 also features an exhibition sapphire crystal case back through which the automatic chronometer movement can be seen.\u003cspan\u003e \u003c\/span\u003eBy 1933 aircraft design had moved forward rapidly, with Boeing at the forefront of innovation. The twin-engined Boeing Model 247 was a major advance in passenger air travel. Used by both civilian and military operators, the Model 247 set the standard for basic airline design for the next decade.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"content__watch__main__features\"\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eModified calibre 13 ¼''' BE-54AE automatic chronometer with 42 hour power reserve\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBoeing aviation-grade Ti 6-4 titanium case\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWater resistant to 10 ATM, 100 metres\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTitanium bracelet and additional strap\u003c\/li\u003e\n\u003c\/ul\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n      \u003c\/div\u003e\n    \u003c\/div\u003e\n    \n    \n    \u003cdiv class=\"product-main-end\"\u003e  \n      \u003cdiv class=\"product-find\"\u003e\n        \u003ca href=\"\/pages\/store-locator\"\u003eFind a store\u003c\/a\u003e\n      \u003c\/div\u003e \n      \n      \n            \u003caside class=\"share-buttons\"\u003e  \u003cdiv class=\"share-buttons--list\"\u003e    \u003ca      class=\"share-buttons--button shar